; jsoo mirror of lib/native. Sources are copied, never forked: see
; .ai/js_backends_design.md and expr-tailcall-implementation-plan.md under
; .ai/ (tail-call conversion, Stage 3). Needed purely so this library's
; global, unqualified [Expr] name binds to [Expr_js] (whose evaluator is
; preprocessed with JS_BACKEND) rather than to ordinary [Expr] -- native's own
; sources are otherwise unchanged and copied verbatim.
;
; Four copy_files stanzas, one per source directory (root, ops/, transform/,
; transform/passes/): copy_files does not recurse, and native's own
; `include_subdirs unqualified` already flattens all four into one namespace,
; so the mirror does the same by copying every directory's files into this
; one flat directory. Checked for basename collisions across all four source
; directories (none) before doing this. Wildcard globs are safe for three of
; the four (unlike expr_internal_js): lib/native's active (non-landmarks)
; stanza runs no action-based preprocessing of its own, so there is no
; origin-stanza rule to collide with.
;
; The root stanza is the one exception, and for a DIFFERENT reason than
; expr_internal_js's M1 workaround: dune's copy_files has no glob-exclusion
; syntax, and this mirror must NOT copy lib/native/kernel_hard.ml verbatim --
; see kernel_hard.ml below for why. So the root stanza enumerates every other
; root file explicitly instead of globbing (tail-call plan, Stage 7; see
; .ai/). Add a new lib/native root module to this list, or it is simply
; invisible to native_js.
;
; No landmarks-instrumented variant: js/jsoo never builds under
; `--profile landmarks`, so unlike lib/native/dune this is a single stanza.
;
; The checked-in expr.ml shim (`include Expr_js.Expr`) is the plan's
; documented pattern for every additional Expr consumer -- see .ai/.

; Two brace-alternation globs (dune's `files` field takes exactly one glob
; term, matching experiments/tailcall/jsoo/dune's proven shape): every root
; module WITH an .mli, and every root module WITHOUT one, each minus
; `kernel_hard`. Add a new lib/native root module's basename to whichever
; group matches its shape.

(copy_files
 (files
  %{workspace_root}/lib/native/{aten_int,aten_shape,dim,dim_arith,direct,eval_direct,eval_symbolic,expr_bridge,fusion_plan,graph_builder,graph_ir,graph_ir_op,graph_json,kernel_adapt,kernel_elab,kernel_eval,kernel,op_config,output_ordinal,output_spec,quant,rank,region_computation,region_eval,region_execution,region_group,region_kernel,region_local,region_partition,region_program,region_slots,region_trace,shape_error,slot,stage_program,symbolic,tensor_id,vec6}.{ml,mli}))

(copy_files
 (files
  %{workspace_root}/lib/native/{axis,eval_op,graph_common,graph_shape,half,json_util,kernel_hard_shared,payload,region_context,schedule,semantics,symint,tensor,tensor_ref,tensor_sig,walk_bridge}.ml))

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/lib/native/ops/*.{ml,mli}))

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/lib/native/transform/*.{ml,mli}))

(copy_files
 (files %{workspace_root}/lib/native/transform/passes/*.{ml,mli}))

